# Orbit primary Graphify scope
#
# This is the maintained engineering/current-state graph. It keeps application
# source, tests, living system docs/runbooks, and the root planning summaries.
# Historical, narrative, generated, and agent-infrastructure corpora remain
# searchable in the repo and can be graphed on demand.

# Generated graph artifacts must never graph themselves.
graphify-out/
.planning/graphs/

# Narrative / decision-prep work is a separate corpus. The dossier is orbit's
# authoritative DECISION source, but its long prose and repeated feature
# headings overwhelm engineering community detection when mixed into this graph.
# Its decisions reach the graph via ADRs + the registry, exactly like ADR bodies.
docs/dossier/
docs/audits/
docs/mockups/
docs/personal-todos.md

# Completed phase artifacts and ancillary planning collections are valuable
# history but are frequently superseded. Current truth stays represented by the
# root PROJECT/ROADMAP/REQUIREMENTS files.
#
# STATE.md is excluded despite being a root summary: it is a prepend-log that
# parses into its own meaningless community and churns on every plan.
.planning/STATE.md
.planning/phases/
.planning/debug/
.planning/handoffs/
.planning/research/
.planning/todos/
.planning/sync-milestone/
.planning/knowledgebase/

# Living system docs summarize operative decisions and link back to immutable
# ADRs. Indexing every ADR heading adds thousands of historical document nodes,
# and the graph has no concept of supersession — a retired ADR would sit in the
# corpus with as much authority as the one that replaced it.
#
# INDEX.md and adr-registry.ts are the deliberate exceptions: supersession state
# is IN them, so it stays represented rather than absent. Written as
# `docs/decisions/*` (not `docs/decisions/`) on purpose — gitignore forbids a `!`
# rule from re-including a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so excluding
# the children individually is what keeps the negations below alive.
docs/decisions/*
!docs/decisions/INDEX.md
!docs/decisions/adr-registry.ts

# Agent/runtime infrastructure is not part of the product dependency graph.
.claude/
.codex/
.gsd/
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
